<problem><title>Video review question</title>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<graph size="small">
  <xLabel><m>x</m></xLabel>
  <yLabel><m>f(x)</m></yLabel>
  <function name="f">x/2 + 1
    <label><m>f</m></label>
  </function>
  <line styleNumber="6" fixed="true">x=3</line>
  <point styleNumber="5" fixed="true">(3,5/2)</point>
</graph>
<p>Given the linear function <m>f(x) = $f</m>, what is the slope of the graph of <m>f</m> at <m>x = 3</m>?</p>
  <p><m>f'(3) = </m>
  <answer name="ans1">1/2</answer>.</p>
<hint hide="$ans1.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $ans1.creditAchieved = 1">
  <p>What is the slope of the linear function <m>f(x) = $f</m>?</p>
</hint>
<p>Using the questions below, let's also determine the derivative of <m>f</m> using the derivative formula:</p>
  <p>First we calculate the slope of the secant line between position
    <answer name="ans2" inline="true">
      <choice><m>y_0</m></choice>
      <choice><m>\Delta x</m></choice>
      <choice credit="1"><m>x_0</m></choice>
    </answer> and position
    <answer name="ans3" inline="true">
      <choice><m>y_2</m></choice>
      <choice><m>\Delta x</m></choice>
      <choice credit="1"><m>x_0 + \Delta x</m></choice>
    </answer>.</p>
  <p>The difference <m>(f($ans3) - f($ans2))</m> in the output values between these two points is divided by 
    <answer name="ans4" inline="true">
      <choice><m>y_2</m></choice>
      <choice credit="1"><m>\Delta x</m></choice>
      <choice><m>x_0 + \Delta x</m></choice>
    </answer> to get the secant slope:

    <me>\text{secant slope} = \frac{\Delta f}{\Delta x} = \frac{f($ans3) - f($ans2)}{$ans4} = \frac{1}{2}</me>.</p>
    <p>Finally, we take the 
      <answer name="ans5">
      <choice credit="1"><m>\lim_{\Delta x \to 0}</m></choice>
      <choice>product of <m>\Delta x</m> and <m>\Delta f</m></choice>
      <choice>sum of <m>f($ans3)</m> and <m>f($ans2)</m></choice>
    </answer> of <m>\frac{f($ans3) - f($ans2)}{$ans4}</m> to arrive at the slope of the tangent line of our function,
      <md>
      <mrow>$ans5 \amp= \frac{\Delta f}{\Delta x} = $ans5 \frac{f($ans3) - f($ans2)}{$ans4}</mrow>
        <mrow>\amp=$ans5 \frac{1}{2} </mrow>
        <mrow> \amp= \frac{1}{2}.</mrow>
      </md></p>
      <p>The derivative of the function <m>f</m> at <m>x = 3</m> is <m>f'(3) = </m> <answer name="ans6">1/2</answer>.</p>
<hint hide="$ans6.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $ans6.creditAchieved = 1">
  <p>What is the slope of the linear function $f? Since the slope of a linear function is constant, its derivative is also a constant value. So, since <m>f'(x) = \frac{1}{2}</m> for all <m>x</m>, <m>f'(3)</m> for <m>x = 3</m> is...</p>
</hint>

</exercise>
</problem>

